<file path="VERCEL_DEPLOY.md">
# Vercel Deployment Guide — PyQuant Control Center (API + Frontend)

This is the complete, step-by-step procedure for deploying `api/index.py`
+ `web/` to Vercel as the project `pyq-p3` (`https://pyq-p3.vercel.app`).
Follow it top to bottom on a fresh checkout — every step is included, not
just the ones that differ from "obvious" defaults.

**Why the earlier deploy 404'd on every path** (both `/` and `/api/health`):
the repo's `vercel.json` had a `"rewrites"` block pointing `/api/*` at
`/api/index.py` — but Vercel's legacy file-based model routes a function
at `api/index.py` to the path `/api` (no `.py`, no `/index` suffix), so
that rewrite's destination never matched anything real. On top of that,
`requirements.txt` at the repo root listed `fastapi`, which risks Vercel
auto-detecting the **Python framework preset** (a different routing model
where one app handles every request) while `vercel.json` was still written
for the **old file-based model** — two incompatible routing assumptions
active at once. The fix below commits fully to the framework-preset model:
`pyproject.toml`'s `[tool.vercel].entrypoint` tells Vercel exactly which
app to load, `api/index.py` itself now serves the static frontend via a
`StaticFiles` mount (so one app truly can answer everything), and
`vercel.json` is now just `{}` — no rewrites, no per-file function config,
nothing left to contradict the framework preset.

---

## Part A — One-time local tool setup

### A1. Confirm Node.js is installed (needed for the Vercel CLI)

Open PowerShell or Command Prompt on your Windows machine and run:

```
node --version
```

- If you see a version number (e.g. `v20.11.0`), skip to A2.
- If you see `'node' is not recognized...`, install Node.js:
  1. Go to https://nodejs.org in your browser.
  2. Download the **LTS** installer for Windows (the left-hand button).
  3. Run the downloaded `.msi` file, accept all defaults, click through
     the installer (Next → Next → Install → Finish).
  4. Close and reopen your terminal (PowerShell/Command Prompt) so it
     picks up the new install.
  5. Run `node --version` again to confirm it now prints a version.

### A2. Install the Vercel CLI

```
npm install -g vercel
```

Confirm it installed:

```
vercel --version
```

You should see a version number (e.g. `35.x.x`). If you instead see
`'vercel' is not recognized`, close and reopen your terminal and try again
— npm's global install path is usually only picked up by new terminal
sessions.

### A3. Log in to Vercel from the CLI

```
vercel login
```

This prints a prompt asking for your email, then sends a confirmation
link to that email address (or opens a browser for a one-click login,
depending on CLI version). Open the email/browser link, confirm, then
return to the terminal — it will print `> Success! ...` once logged in.

---

## Part B — Link this repo to the existing `pyq-p3` Vercel project

Since `pyq-p3.vercel.app` already exists (it's the project that 404'd),
you're linking your local folder to that **existing** project, not
creating a new one.

### B1. Open a terminal in the repo folder

```
cd C:\Users\Pyrex\pyq-p3
```

(Adjust the path if your checkout lives somewhere else — it must be the
folder that directly contains `vercel.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `api/`,
and `web/`.)

### B2. Run the link command

```
vercel link
```

It will ask a series of questions — answer exactly as follows:

1. `? Set up and deploy "C:\Users\Pyrex\pyq-p3"?` → type `Y`, press Enter.
2. `? Which scope should contain your project?` → select your account
   (use arrow keys, press Enter).
3. `? Link to existing project?` → type `Y`, press Enter.
4. `? What's the name of your existing project?` → type `pyq-p3`, press
   Enter.

It will confirm with something like `✅ Linked to <you>/pyq-p3`. This
creates a local `.vercel/` folder (already in `.gitignore`) that remembers
this link for future `vercel` commands.

---

## Part C — Set environment variables

Your FastAPI backend reads these at runtime (see `api/index.py`'s
`/api/config` endpoint for the full list it checks). The **only one that
actually matters for the API to function correctly** is `DATABASE_URL` —
without it, the API falls back to a local SQLite file that resets on
every deploy (Vercel's filesystem is ephemeral), so the UI would never
show persisted signals/runs. The rest (`ALPACA_*`, `BYBIT_*`,
`BINANCE_*`, `TELEGRAM_*`) are optional — they only drive the masked
"is this configured?" checkmarks on the Settings screen and are never
used by the API to call any exchange.

Set at minimum:

| Variable | Value |
|---|---|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Your Supabase **direct connection** string (see `SUPABASE_SETUP.md`) |
| `FRONTEND_ORIGIN` | `https://pyq-p3.vercel.app` (tightens CORS; `*` also works if you'd rather skip this) |
| `PYQUANT_MODE` | `live` or `paper` — purely informational on this API; matches whatever your VPS orchestra process is actually running under |

### C1. Option 1 — CLI (fastest)

Run each of these from the repo root (replace the `<...>` placeholders).
Each command will prompt `? What's the value of DATABASE_URL?` — paste the
value and press Enter, then it asks which environments (`Production`,
`Preview`, `Development`) — press `a` to select all, then Enter.

```
vercel env add DATABASE_URL
vercel env add FRONTEND_ORIGIN
vercel env add PYQUANT_MODE
```

### C2. Option 2 — Dashboard (click-through alternative, no CLI)

1. Open https://vercel.com/dashboard in your browser and log in.
2. Click the **pyq-p3** project card.
3. Click the **Settings** tab (top nav bar of the project page).
4. Click **Environment Variables** in the left-hand sidebar.
5. For each variable in the table above:
   a. In the **Key** field, type the variable name exactly (e.g.
      `DATABASE_URL`).
   b. In the **Value** field, paste the value.
   c. Under **Environments**, tick all three boxes: Production, Preview,
      Development.
   d. Click **Save**.
6. Repeat for all three variables.

---

## Part D — Deploy

### D1. Deploy to production

From the repo root:

```
vercel --prod
```

This uploads the current local files (not a git push — your earlier
GitHub push block doesn't affect this at all) and builds/deploys them.
Wait for it to print a line like:

```
✅  Production: https://pyq-p3.vercel.app [copied to clipboard]
```

If the build fails, the CLI prints the error inline — re-read it
carefully; the most common cause after this fix would be a typo in
`pyproject.toml`. You can also inspect the build in the dashboard: go to
the project page → **Deployments** tab → click the newest (top) row →
**Build Logs**.

### D2. Confirm the Framework Preset Vercel detected

1. In the dashboard, go to **pyq-p3** → **Settings** → **General**.
2. Scroll to **Build & Development Settings**.
3. Confirm **Framework Preset** shows a Python-based preset (not
   "Other" with no framework detected). If it shows "Other", click
   **Edit**, and if a Python option isn't offered in the dropdown, this
   usually self-corrects once `pyproject.toml` exists at the root for the
   *next* deploy — re-run `vercel --prod --force` (the `--force` flag
   skips Vercel's build cache, guaranteeing it re-reads `pyproject.toml`
   from scratch).

---

## Part E — Verify

Run each of these from PowerShell/Command Prompt:

```
curl https://pyq-p3.vercel.app/api/health
```
Expected: `{"ok":true}`

```
curl https://pyq-p3.vercel.app/api/status
```
Expected: `{"trading_enabled":true,"mode":"live"}` (or `"paper"`, matching
whatever you set `PYQUANT_MODE` to).

Then open `https://pyq-p3.vercel.app/` in a browser — you should see the
Dashboard page render (not a 404 JSON blob). Click through to
`/signals.html`, `/backtest.html`, `/settings.html`, `/live-monitor.html`
from the page's own nav links and confirm each one loads.

If `/api/dashboard` shows all-empty data (`"open_positions":[]`,
`"last_run":null`), that's expected until the VPS orchestra process
(`VPS_SETUP.md`) has actually run at least once and written to the
`DATABASE_URL` you configured above — the API is working correctly, it
just has nothing logged yet.

---

## Troubleshooting

- **Still 404 on every path after `vercel --prod`:** run
  `vercel --prod --force` to bypass the build cache entirely, then repeat
  Part E. Also double check `vercel.json`'s content is exactly `{}` — if
  any leftover `"rewrites"` or `"functions"` key is present, delete it.
- **404 only on `/api/...` paths, `/` works fine:** confirms the static
  mount works but the API routes aren't registering — check
  **Deployments → (latest) → Build Logs** for a Python import error (most
  likely a missing dependency not listed in `pyproject.toml`'s
  `dependencies` array).
- **500 error on any `/api/...` route:** check
  **Deployments → (latest) → Functions** (or **Runtime Logs**) tab in the
  dashboard — this shows the actual Python traceback. The most common
  cause is `DATABASE_URL` being set but malformed (see
  `SUPABASE_SETUP.md`'s "Build your `DATABASE_URL`" section for the exact
  format) or `psycopg2` failing to connect because the Supabase project
  is paused (free-tier Supabase projects pause after a week of
  inactivity — open the Supabase dashboard once to un-pause it).
- **Environment variable changes don't seem to take effect:** env var
  changes in the dashboard do **not** apply to already-built deployments
  — you must trigger a new deploy afterward (`vercel --prod` again, or in
  the dashboard: **Deployments** → latest row → **⋯** menu → **Redeploy**).
</file>

<file path="web/assets/app.js">
/* PyQuant Control Center — shared frontend logic.
 *
 * This is a genuinely separate, deployable static frontend (plain HTML/CSS/
 * JS) — NOT an edit to the Design-canvas .dc.html mockup. It fetches real
 * data from the Phase 2 FastAPI backend (api/index.py) over HTTP.
 *
 * API base resolution, in order:
 *   1. window.PYQUANT_API_BASE set inline on the page (useful for a
 *      two-project deploy: static site on one Vercel project, API on
 *      another).
 *   2. "/api" — the default, correct when the frontend and API share one
 *      Vercel project (vercel.json's rewrite routes /api/* to api/index.py
 *      already; this is the zero-config path).
 */
const API_BASE = window.PYQUANT_API_BASE || "/api";

async function apiGet(path, params) {
  const url = new URL(API_BASE + path, window.location.origin);
  if (params) {
    Object.entries(params).forEach(([k, v]) => {
      if (v !== undefined && v !== null && v !== "") url.searchParams.set(k, v);
    });
  }
  const res = await fetch(url.toString());
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`GET ${path} failed: ${res.status}`);
  return res.json();
}

async function apiPost(path, body) {
  const res = await fetch(API_BASE + path, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify(body || {}),
  });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`POST ${path} failed: ${res.status}`);
  return res.json();
}

function fmtMoney(v) {
  if (v === null || v === undefined) return "—";
  const n = Number(v);
  const sign = n > 0 ? "+" : "";
  return `${sign}$${n.toFixed(2)}`;
}

function fmtPrice(v) {
  if (v === null || v === undefined) return "—";
  return Number(v).toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
}

function fmtTime(v) {
  if (!v) return "—";
  try {
    const d = new Date(v);
    return d.toLocaleString(undefined, {
      month: "short", day: "numeric", hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit",
    });
  } catch {
    return v;
  }
}

function pnlClass(v) {
  if (v === null || v === undefined) return "";
  return Number(v) >= 0 ? "pnl-pos" : "pnl-neg";
}

function statusLabel(status) {
  const map = {
    open: "OPEN", closed_tp: "TP HIT", closed_sl: "SL HIT", closed_manual: "CLOSED",
  };
  return map[status] || status.toUpperCase();
}

/** Renders the LIVE/PAPER/OFF switch in the topbar and wires the OFF toggle
 *  to POST /api/status. LIVE/PAPER are shown as the orchestra's current
 *  configured mode (informational — see api/index.py's /api/status
 *  docstring for why switching exchange credentials isn't done from here);
 *  OFF is the one real, live control. */
async function mountModeSwitch(containerId) {
  const el = document.getElementById(containerId);
  if (!el) return;
  try {
    const status = await apiGet("/status");
    renderModeSwitch(el, status);
  } catch (e) {
    el.innerHTML = `<span style="color:var(--text-faint); font-size:12px;">status unavailable</span>`;
  }
}

function renderModeSwitch(el, status) {
  const mode = status.mode === "paper" ? "PAPER" : "LIVE";
  const enabled = status.trading_enabled;
  el.innerHTML = `
    <button type="button" class="${mode === 'LIVE' ? 'active' : ''}" disabled>LIVE</button>
    <button type="button" class="${mode === 'PAPER' ? 'active' : ''}" disabled>PAPER</button>
    <button type="button" id="off-toggle" class="${!enabled ? 'off active' : ''}">
      ${enabled ? 'TURN OFF' : 'OFF (tap to resume)'}
    </button>
  `;
  const toggle = el.querySelector("#off-toggle");
  toggle.addEventListener("click", async () => {
    toggle.disabled = true;
    try {
      const next = await apiPost("/status", { enabled: !enabled });
      renderModeSwitch(el, next);
    } catch (e) {
      toggle.disabled = false;
      alert("Could not update trading switch: " + e.message);
    }
  });
}

function highlightActiveNav() {
  const here = window.location.pathname.split("/").pop() || "index.html";
  document.querySelectorAll("nav.primary a").forEach((a) => {
    const href = a.getAttribute("href");
    if (href === here) a.classList.add("active");
  });
}

document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
  highlightActiveNav();
  mountModeSwitch("mode-switch");
});
</file>

<file path="web/assets/style.css">
/* PyQuant Control Center — shared stylesheet
   Color tokens matched to the approved Design-canvas mockup
   (Main.dc.html / LiveMonitor.dc.html / Signals.dc.html / Backtest.dc.html /
   ApiKeys.dc.html) so this deployable frontend reads as the same product,
   not a re-skin. This file is hand-written, separate production CSS — the
   mockup's own .dc.html files are a Claude-hosted design reference, not
   something this frontend imports or extends. */

:root {
  --bg: #0B0D11;
  --bg-panel: #12151A;
  --border: #242933;
  --border-soft: #171B22;
  --text: #E7E9ED;
  --text-dim: #C9CDD4;
  --text-muted: #8A909C;
  --text-faint: #565C68;
  --accent: #5B8DEF;
  --accent-soft: #2C3B5C;
  --accent-soft-text: #BBD0FF;
  --green: #3FB950;
  --red: #F2545B;
  --amber: #E3A13A;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; }

html, body {
  margin: 0;
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
}

.mono { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; }

a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
a:hover { color: #7fa4f3; }

::-webkit-scrollbar { width: 8px; height: 8px; }
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb { background: var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 13px; }
th {
  color: var(--text-faint); font-weight: 500; text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em; font-size: 11px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
}
td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft); color: var(--text-dim); }
tbody tr:hover td { background: #0E1116; }

.app-shell {
  min-height: 100vh; width: 100%; max-width: 1440px; margin: 0 auto;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: var(--bg);
}

.topbar {
  height: 64px; flex: 0 0 auto; display: flex; align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between; padding: 0 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  background: var(--bg); position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10;
}

.brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
.brand .name { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.01em; }
.brand .subtitle { color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 13px; margin-left: 2px; }

.mode-switch {
  display: flex; gap: 4px; background: var(--bg-panel); border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 8px; padding: 3px;
}
.mode-switch button {
  font-family: inherit; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 6px; border: none; background: transparent;
  color: var(--text-muted); cursor: pointer; transition: background .12s, color .12s;
}
.mode-switch button.active { background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent-soft-text); }
.mode-switch button.off.active { background: #4a2328; color: #ffb3b8; }

nav.primary { display: flex; gap: 20px; padding: 0 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
nav.primary a {
  display: inline-block; padding: 12px 2px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted);
  border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
}
nav.primary a:hover { color: var(--text); }
nav.primary a.active { color: var(--text); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

main { padding: 24px; flex: 1 1 auto; }

.grid { display: grid; gap: 16px; }
.cols-2 { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
.cols-3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
.cols-4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .cols-2, .cols-3, .cols-4 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

.card {
  background: var(--bg-panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 18px 20px;
}
.card h3 {
  margin: 0 0 14px 0; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: var(--text-faint); font-weight: 600;
}

.stat-value { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; }
.stat-label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 4px; }

.pill {
  display: inline-block; padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px;
  font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}
.pill.open { background: #1c2f52; color: #8fb4ff; }
.pill.closed_tp { background: #113524; color: #6fd99a; }
.pill.closed_sl { background: #40201f; color: #ff9a92; }
.pill.closed_manual { background: #2a2a1f; color: #e0d27a; }

.side-buy { color: var(--green); }
.side-sell { color: var(--red); }
.pnl-pos { color: var(--green); }
.pnl-neg { color: var(--red); }

.empty-state { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; padding: 24px; text-align: center; }

.config-row {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 11px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
}
.config-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
.config-key { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-dim); }
.dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-block; margin-right: 8px; }
.dot.set { background: var(--green); }
.dot.unset { background: var(--text-faint); }

.banner {
  padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
}
.banner.warn { background: #3a2a14; color: #e3b96a; border: 1px solid #5a4322; }
.banner.error { background: #3a1416; color: #ff9a92; border: 1px solid #5a2224; }

footer.hint { padding: 16px 24px; color: var(--text-faint); font-size: 12px; }
</file>

<file path="web/backtest.html">
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>PyQuant — Backtest</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./assets/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="app-shell">
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="brand">
      <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 17L9 11L13 15L21 7" stroke="#5B8DEF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M15 7H21V13" stroke="#5B8DEF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      <span class="name">PyQuant</span>
      <span class="subtitle">Control Center</span>
    </div>
    <div class="mode-switch" id="mode-switch"></div>
  </header>
  <nav class="primary">
    <a href="index.html">Dashboard</a>
    <a href="live-monitor.html">Live Monitor</a>
    <a href="signals.html">Signals</a>
    <a href="backtest.html">Backtest</a>
    <a href="settings.html">API Keys &amp; Settings</a>
  </nav>
  <main>
    <div id="banner-slot"></div>
    <div class="grid cols-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Walkforward Runs</h3>
        <table id="tbl-wf">
          <thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Return</th><th>Win Rate</th><th>Trades</th><th>Finished</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="empty-state" id="empty-wf" style="display:none;">
          No walkforward runs logged yet — run <code class="mono">python3 walkforward.py</code> to log one.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Daily Optimizer Runs</h3>
        <table id="tbl-opt">
          <thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>BTC bal</th><th>ETH bal</th><th>Finished</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="empty-state" id="empty-opt" style="display:none;">
          No optimizer runs logged yet — these are recorded automatically by p4_orchestra.py's daily 00:03 job.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:16px;" id="detail-card" style="display:none;">
      <h3>Run Detail</h3>
      <pre id="detail-pre" class="mono" style="white-space:pre-wrap; color:var(--text-dim); font-size:12px;"></pre>
    </div>
  </main>
  <footer class="hint">Click a run to see its full metrics/params payload.</footer>
</div>
<script src="./assets/app.js"></script>
<script>
async function showDetail(runId) {
  const card = document.getElementById("detail-card");
  const pre = document.getElementById("detail-pre");
  try {
    const run = await apiGet(`/runs/${runId}`);
    pre.textContent = JSON.stringify(run, null, 2);
    card.style.display = "block";
  } catch (e) {
    pre.textContent = "Could not load run: " + e.message;
    card.style.display = "block";
  }
}

async function loadRuns() {
  const bannerSlot = document.getElementById("banner-slot");
  try {
    const wf = await apiGet("/runs", { run_type: "walkforward" });
    const wfBody = document.querySelector("#tbl-wf tbody");
    if (wf.runs.length === 0) {
      document.getElementById("empty-wf").style.display = "block";
    } else {
      wfBody.innerHTML = wf.runs.map(r => {
        const m = r.metrics || {};
        return `
        <tr style="cursor:pointer;" onclick="showDetail(${r.id})">
          <td class="mono">#${r.id}</td>
          <td class="mono">${m["Total Return (%)"] ?? "—"}%</td>
          <td class="mono">${m["Win Rate (%)"] ?? "—"}%</td>
          <td class="mono">${m["Total Trades"] ?? "—"}</td>
          <td>${fmtTime(r.finished_at)}</td>
        </tr>`;
      }).join("");
    }

    const opt = await apiGet("/runs", { run_type: "daily_optimizer" });
    const optBody = document.querySelector("#tbl-opt tbody");
    if (opt.runs.length === 0) {
      document.getElementById("empty-opt").style.display = "block";
    } else {
      optBody.innerHTML = opt.runs.map(r => {
        const m = r.metrics || {};
        return `
        <tr style="cursor:pointer;" onclick="showDetail(${r.id})">
          <td class="mono">#${r.id}</td>
          <td class="mono">${fmtMoney(m.btc_val)}</td>
          <td class="mono">${fmtMoney(m.eth_val)}</td>
          <td>${fmtTime(r.finished_at)}</td>
        </tr>`;
      }).join("");
    }
  } catch (e) {
    bannerSlot.innerHTML = `<div class="banner error">Could not reach the API (${e.message}).</div>`;
  }
}
loadRuns();
</script>
</body>
</html>
</file>

